-- title:
--   Open cubes are open sets
-- statement:
--   For $h > 0$ and $u \in \mathbb{R}^d$, the cube
--   $$A_h(u) \;=\; \bigl\{x \in \mathbb{R}^d : \|x-u\|_\infty < \tfrac h2\bigr\},
--   \qquad \|x\|_\infty = \sup_i |x_i|,$$
--   of centre $u$ and side length $h$ is an open subset of $\mathbb{R}^d$.
--
--   This is the counterpart of the closedness of the closed cube; openness gives measurability and, more usefully, means the cube is a neighbourhood of each of its points, so that any point of $A_h(u)$ has a whole ball of companions inside the cube.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The hypothesis is strict positivity of the side length $h$, and the ambient topology is the Euclidean one on `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)` while the cube is defined through the maximum norm.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/LebesgueDiff.lean#L57-L60

